  "DE_minijob": {
   "country": "DE",
   "cause": "Minijob boundary (6,672 euros a year, 556 a month): below it the pay is taxed flat by the employer and stays out of the joint assessment, and the employee pays no contributions in the model; one euro more puts the whole pay into the couple's splitting tariff (married: -1,509 euros) and, for the childless, starts the care-insurance surcharge (0.6 points), charged on the transition zone's whole contribution base (about 372 euros a month at the boundary) where the employee's own share starts from nothing (childless single: -26 euros for 1 euro; with a child the step is 0.30 euros a year)",
   "law": "EStG § 40a (2), § 40 (3); SGB IV § 8 (1a), § 20 (2a); SGB XI § 55 (3), § 58 (1)",
